---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Icon from '../components/Icon.astro';
import Closing from '../components/Closing.astro';
import CampaignParagraphs from '../components/CampaignParagraphs.astro';
import { factSheetSections, faqs, paragraphText } from '../data/campaign';
const faqSchema = {
  '@type': 'FAQPage',
  mainEntity: faqs.map(faq => ({
    '@type': 'Question', name: faq.question,
    acceptedAnswer: { '@type': 'Answer', text: paragraphText(faq.paragraphs) },
  })),
};
---
<Layout title="Facts & FAQ" seoTitle="Pasadena Measure PFD: 2026 Fire Parcel Tax & FAQ" description="What is the Pasadena fire tax? Get Measure PFD costs, exemptions, fire funding, and Yes/No voting facts for the 2026 parcel tax proposal. From the No campaign." structuredData={faqSchema}>
  <section class="page-intro container">
    <h1>What is Pasadena<br />Measure PFD?</h1>

  </section>
  <section class="container facts-overview" id="overview" aria-labelledby="overview-title">
    <h2 id="overview-title">What is the proposed Pasadena fire tax?</h2>
    <div class="reference-answer"><p><strong>Measure PFD is a proposed Pasadena fire tax on the November 3, 2026 ballot.</strong> It would charge $0.19 per square foot of improved property annually, subject to exemptions, and expire 14 years after its effective date unless extended by voters. Funds would support specified fire facilities, equipment, and emergency-response services.</p><p>A <strong>Yes vote</strong> supports adopting the proposed tax. A <strong>No vote</strong> opposes adopting it. Passage requires at least two-thirds of votes cast on Measure PFD. <a href="/measure-pfd-pass-or-fail/">See what voting Yes or No on Measure PFD means</a>.</p></div>
    <div class="overview-details">
      <div class="overview-detail"><h3 id="costs" class="section-anchor">How much would Measure PFD cost?</h3><p>It would cost $0.19 per taxable square foot each year, before exemptions. For 1,600 square feet, that is $304 a year.</p><p><a href="/measure-pfd-calculator/">Calculate your PFD tax increase</a>.</p></div>
      <div class="overview-detail"><h3 id="exemptions" class="section-anchor">Who qualifies for a Measure PFD exemption?</h3><p>Exemptions would cover qualifying low-income owners, owners with specified senior or disability utility-tax exemptions, government property, and qualifying religious or community-service property.</p><p><a href="/measure-pfd-exemptions/">Check your PFD exemptions</a>.</p></div>
      <div class="overview-detail"><h3 id="funding" class="section-anchor">What fire services would PFD fund?</h3><p>It would fund fire facilities, including rebuilding Stations 33 and 37, equipment, and emergency-response improvements.</p><p><a href="/measure-pfd-fire-station-funding/">Explore Measure PFD funding for Pasadena firefighters and stations</a>, or <a href="/measure-pfd-vs-measure-i/">compare PFD with Measure I</a>.</p></div>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="container ballot-reference" id="ballot-information" aria-labelledby="ballot-information-title">
    <h2 id="ballot-information-title">How does Measure PFD appear on the ballot?</h2>
    <p>The official title is <strong>City of Pasadena 911 Firefighter/Paramedic Emergency Medical/Wildfire Preparedness/Response Measure</strong>. The ballot question describes a proposed tax expected to raise approximately $22.1 million annually for specified local fire and emergency-response purposes.</p>
    <p>Read the <a href="https://www.cityofpasadena.net/city-clerk/wp-content/uploads/sites/21/2026-General-Election-Ballot-Measure-Information.pdf#page=3" type="application/pdf">official ballot question and ordinance (PDF)</a> and the <a href="https://www.cityofpasadena.net/fire/wp-content/uploads/sites/25/Measure-PFD-City-Attorney-Impartial-Analysis.pdf" type="application/pdf">City Attorney’s impartial analysis (PDF)</a>. To compare the funding rationale and our campaign’s objections, read the <a href="/measure-pfd-pass-or-fail/#arguments">Measure PFD pros and cons</a>.</p>
  </section>
  <section id="resources" class="container resource-hub section-anchor" aria-labelledby="resources-title">
    <h2 id="resources-title">Looking for more detail?</h2>
    <p>Estimate your added tax, understand your property-tax bill, or read why others oppose Measure PFD.</p>
    <a class="button button-outline secondary-action" href="/resources/">Browse all resources</a>
  </section>
  <section id="questions" class="faq-section section-anchor">
    <div class="container faq-layout">
      <div class="section-heading"><h2>Answers about<br />Measure PFD.</h2><p>Our answers to questions about costs, fairness, and fire funding.</p></div>
      <div class="faq-list">{faqs.map(faq => <details class="faq-item section-anchor" id={faq.id}>
        <summary><span>{faq.question}</span><span class="faq-toggle"><Icon name="chevronDown" /></span></summary>
        <div class="faq-answer"><CampaignParagraphs paragraphs={faq.paragraphs} /></div>
      </details>)}</div>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section id="measure" class="facts-section container section-anchor">
    <div class="section-heading"><h2>Campaign<br />fact sheet.</h2><p>Support Firefighters. Stop the Unfair Tax.</p></div>
    <div class="fact-sheet-copy">
      {factSheetSections.map(section => <article class="fact-sheet-section"><h3>{section.title}</h3><CampaignParagraphs paragraphs={section.paragraphs} /></article>)}
      <p class="fact-sheet-closing"><strong>Support Firefighters. Vote NO on Measure PFD.</strong><br />PFDNo.com</p>
    </div>
  </section>
  <p class="container publisher-note">Published by the No on Measure PFD campaign.</p>
  <Closing />
</Layout>

<style>
  .ballot-reference { padding-bottom: 40px; }
  .ballot-reference h2 { margin-bottom: var(--space-copy); font-size: clamp(28px, 3vw, 40px); }
  .ballot-reference p { color: var(--green-soft); }
  .publisher-note { font-size: 14px; line-height: 1.7; padding-bottom: 32px; color: var(--green-soft); }
  .facts-overview .reference-answer { max-width: none; }
  .overview-details { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr)); gap: 32px; margin-block: 32px; }
  .overview-detail { border-top: 1px solid var(--line); padding-top: 24px; }
  .overview-detail h3 { margin: 0 0 16px; }
  .overview-detail p { color: var(--green-soft); }
  @media (max-width: 800px) {
    .overview-details { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 24px; }
  }
  .resource-hub { display: grid; grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) auto; align-items: center; gap: var(--space-copy) var(--space-content); padding-block: 40px 56px; border-top: 1px solid var(--line); }
  .resource-hub h2 { font-size: clamp(30px, 4vw, 42px); margin: 0; }
  .resource-hub > p { grid-column: 1 / -1; grid-row: 2; color: var(--green-soft); max-width: none; }
  .resource-hub > .secondary-action { grid-column: 2; grid-row: 1; margin: 0; justify-self: end; }
  @media (max-width: 800px) {
    .resource-hub { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    .resource-hub > .secondary-action { grid-column: 1; grid-row: 3; }
  }
  .fact-sheet-copy { min-width: 0; font-size: 18px; line-height: 1.75; color: var(--green-soft); }
  .fact-sheet-section + .fact-sheet-section { margin-top: 32px; padding-top: 32px; border-top: 1px solid var(--line); }
  .fact-sheet-section h3 { color: var(--green); font-size: 24px; line-height: 1.3; margin-bottom: 16px; }
  .fact-sheet-closing { margin-top: 32px; color: var(--green); }
  .faq-list > .faq-item:first-child { border-top: 1px solid #cdd5e1; }
  @media screen and (min-width: 801px) {
    .facts-section > .section-heading,
    .faq-layout > .section-heading { position: sticky; top: 150px; align-self: start; }
  }
</style>
